## Storing concentrate

Keep it in a sealed jar or bottle in the fridge. It tastes best in the first week, and most people say it keeps for up to about two weeks, though it slowly gets flatter. If it tastes sour or off, toss it.

A trick worth knowing: pour some concentrate into an ice cube tray and freeze it. Coffee ice cubes don't water your drink down as they melt.

## Tips

- **Use a coarse grind.** Fine grounds make it bitter and are a pain to strain.
- **Strain well.** The fine particles left in it keep extracting in the fridge, so a paper filter helps it keep longer.
- **It's strong.** Cold brew concentrate has a lot of caffeine per ounce, so dilute it before you drink it.
